From 7f7e7a3c32ad22e25809852c42b5f519f78ab3cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:25:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ccci: validate runtime LK metadata before publishing modem
 arguments

Bound descriptor prefixes and signed version/count fields before mapping
LK's full 64 KiB no-map reservation. Validate each consumed tag header,
name, payload range and chain link before publishing any LK arguments.
Preserve existing DT priority and first-wins duplicate behavior, preflight
the finite argument table and roll back partial publication on failure.

Malformed supplied metadata cannot enter the legacy fallback or enable the
modem. Valid no-image sentinels skip dependent parsers. Keep the existing
permanent util module loaded because its logger already registered proc
callbacks. Retain successful read-only mappings while argument entries refer
to them, and make diagnostic dumping bounded and non-mutating.

The descriptor and tag layouts retain the vendor little-endian contract;
this changes input boundaries, not tag payload interpretation or modem
startup policy.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules/tree/3c4ccd07d5624879555ec710c11bb8818e5cb5c6
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
